.TH "ROARK\-SIMULATION\-GROUP\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-simulation-group-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-simulation\-group\-create \- Create a simulation group
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark simulation group create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Saves a named set of plans to run together, again and again. Nothing runs yet: POST /v1/simulation/group/{groupId}/run starts one run of every plan and groups them into a run group with one combined report. Slack channels need Slack connected to the project. Email is on by default.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/simulation/group
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
What to call the group. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
What the group is for. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-simulation\-run\-plan\-ids\fR \fI<value>\fR
The plans to run together, in run order (2 to 20). Duplicates are dropped. Repeatable. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-notifications\fR \fI<value>\fR
Where each run's group report announces itself once it is ready. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-notifications.email\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-notifications.slack\fR \fI<value>\fR
Channels in the project's connected Slack workspace to post the report to (at most 10). Slack must be connected to the project first. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
